            "body": "Clean bug fix.\n\n**Problem**: `quant_config.get(\"format\", \"\").lower()` throws `AttributeError` when `format` is a list (mixed-scheme checkpoints).\n\n**Fix is correct**\n\n- `_compressed_tensors_has_nvfp4()` handles both string and list: `isinstance(fmt, list) ? fmt : [fmt]` gives a uniform iterable.\n- `any(isinstance(f, str) and \"nvfp4\" in f.lower() for f in formats)` is defensive — the tests cover malformed entries (`None`, `4`) in the list.\n- Extracting to a dedicated function mirrors the existing `_modelopt_mixed_has_nvfp4()` pattern, keeping the `is_nvfp4_quantized()` body clean.\n\n**Note on #55367**\n\nGood that you flagged the complementary PR. Whoever lands second will need to guard `_modelopt_mixed_has_nvfp4` against list formats too. Consider cross-referencing both PRs in an issue so reviewers know about the potential conflict.",
