    "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #60260.\n\nMixed-scheme compressed-tensors checkpoints declare the top-level `format` as a list, e.g. `[\"nvfp4-pack-quantized\", \"float-quantized\"]` (`nm-testing/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0-NVFP4-FP8-Dynamic`). `ModelConfig.is_nvfp4_quantized()` called `.lower()` on it, so building the config failed with `AttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'lower'`. That happens when `enable_act_fusion` computes the optimization-level defaults, before any weights load.\n\nThis PR moves the compressed-tensors check into `_compressed_tensors_has_nvfp4()`, next to the existing `_modelopt_mixed_has_nvfp4()` helper, and accepts either a string or a list. Single-string behaviour is unchanged.\n\n## Not a duplicate\n\n- No open PR references #60260.\n- #55367 changes the same function to detect NVFP4 groups in `\"mixed-precision\"` checkpoints. It still calls `quant_config.get(\"format\", \"\").lower()`, so it doesn't cover a list-typed `format`. The two changes are complementary; whichever lands second needs a small rebase.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```\npytest tests/config/test_compressed_tensors_nvfp4.py tests/config/test_modelopt_mixed_nvfp4.py\nruff check / ruff format --check (ruff 0.14.0) on the changed files\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n- 16 passed: 10 new tests for string, list, non-NVFP4 and malformed formats, plus the 6 existing ModelOpt mixed tests.\n- Ruff is clean.\n- Reproduced the crash on the current nightly (`0.30.1rc1.dev740`) with the checkpoint above on an RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell (sm_120).\n\n## AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used in preparing and validating this PR. I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n",
